===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|welde}}, {{m|enm|wolde}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*walþō}} (compare {{cog|nl|wouw}}, {{cog|gml|walde}}, {{m|gml|wolde}}, ''[[gaude]]'' in French), from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*walþuz||forest}}. More at {{l|en|wold}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|wold}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[herb]] ({{taxlink|Reseda luteola|species|noshow=1}}) related to [[mignonette]], growing in Europe, and to some extent in America, used to make a yellow dye.
# The yellow coloring matter or dye extracted from this plant.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|Reseda luteola}} {{l|en|dyer's rocket}}; {{vern|dyer's weed}}; {{vern|wild woad}}

