===Etymology 2===
Alteration of {{m|en|well||boil, rise}}, probably influenced by the past participle, {{m|en|welled|}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To bind together [[inseparably]]; to [[unite]] closely or [[intimately]].
#* '''1847''': [[w:Alfred Lord Tennyson|Alfred Lord Tennyson]], ''The Princess''
#*: Now should men see / Two women faster '''welded''' in one love / Than pairs of wedlock.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[join]] two [[material]]s (especially two [[metal]]s) together by applying [[heat]], [[pressure]] and [[filler]], either separately or in any combination.

